  The cosine column must be FLAT across scratch counts. It is the same
  circuit with parities on different wires, so any drift is a bookkeeping
  error rather than a trade.

  Depth should fall and 2q should rise. Worth taking only if some scratch
  count gets depth near the one-hot row WITHOUT giving back the 6x circuit
  advantage or the two-qubit advantage.
